Can you make a CoreWars warrior that always loses, no ties? 

The solution is simple. The challenge will give you a imp.red file that you would need to download and navigate through in the filepath using the terminal.

For example, since I am using a UNIX system, and my downloads will be in the /Downloads directory, I would navigate there by running the command:

cd /Downloads

Then, I would inspect the imp.red file by running

cat imp.red

This gives the output

;redcode
;name Imp Ex
;assert 1
mov 0, 1
end

Here, you would need to understand what each lines represent within a .red file. To simplify, anything that starts with a semi-colon (;) would be there to run the code itself. In redcode ; is a comment that the code interprets as metadata.
Understanding this, you would see that only mov 0, 1 is something you would be able to modify (believe me, I tried modifying ;assert 1 to ;assert 0 [the code wouldn't run]).

So by changing it to mov 0, 0 (in other words, running in circles, therefore being harmless)

BOOM! You get the flag.

