So my previous explaination was partially correct because if you changed the value to anything using mov, your character would always lose.

I had to look up the manual for this, and apparently, you can modify the game to another version aswell.

Hats off to this guy : https://medium.com/@khanzjoel55/pico-ctf-2023-writeups-d2dbc3e91511

Essentially, these are the commands present in redcode.

DAT data
MOV move
ADD add
SUB subtract
MUL multiply
DIV divide
MOD modula (remainder of division)
JMP jump
JMZ jump if zero
JMN jump if not zero
DJN decrement, jump if not zero
SPL split execution
SLT skip if less than
CMP compare (see SEQ)
SEQ skip if equal
SNE skip if not equal
NOP no operation

I think I got it now. While the medium link did helped in solving this challenge, I found an easier solution by only using jump. This was far easier after understanding the purpose of the game.

1. The enemy copies your movement Mov 0, 1.
2. The jump 0 makes your Imp immortal because you're recursively jumping to a safe spot.
3. <- 3 means you're jumping behind the computer's memory. A trap you're setting essentially.

My solution:
;redcode
;name Imp Ex
;assert 2
jmp 0, <- 3
end

